# G047 — Web Bot

*v2. See `web-bot.md` for prose: autonomous actor that navigates,
crawling as BFS over link graph, scripted automation as
choreography, same-domain filter as scope restriction, link graph
as the noosphere's explicit structure.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Automated Content Verification

[verify-publications
    IN ORDER TO
        script a bot to navigate the live sites
        assert response codes, titles, and content markers
        and score the verification only if every assertion passed

    @bot <- [web-bot[new]]
    @script <- [bot-script[new {name: "verify-em-site"}]]
                 + [navigate {url: "https://eckenrodemuziekopname.com"}]
                 + [assert   {check: "status:200"}]
                 + [assert   {check: "contains:Eckenrode Muziekopname"}]
                 + [extract  {pattern: "<title>(.*?)</title>",
                               var: "title"}]
                 + [navigate {url: "https://wiki.eckenrodemuziekopname.com"}]
                 + [assert   {check: "status:200"}]

    @results <- [web-bot[execute {bot: @bot, script: @script}]]

    @results
        where every step:success is true
        and @results:variables:title is "Eckenrode Muziekopname"
            -> [report[pass {verification: @results}]]
        otherwise
            -> #verification-failed
                {failed-steps: @results where success is false}
]

---

## Verb Surface

[web-bot
    new
    execute            {bot, script}              ;; -> Results
    crawl              {bot, start-url, policy}    ;; BFS over links
]

[bot-script
    new                {name}
    + navigate         {url}
    + assert           {check}                      ;; status:N, contains:S, regex:R
    + extract          {pattern, var}
    + fill             {selector, value}
    + click            {selector}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: script as stepwise choreography `where` each gates the next

[web-bot[execute {bot: @b, script: @script}]
    IN ORDER TO
        run each step in order, halting on the first failure
        because assertions are the `<-` gates of this choreography

    state <- {page: none, variables: {}}
    for @step in @script:steps
        @step:kind
            where "navigate"
                -> load @step:url; update state:page
            where "assert"
                -> evaluate @step:check against state:page
                   where true  -> continue
                   otherwise    -> return #failed-at-step @step
            where "extract"
                -> run regex; store group 1 at @step:var in state:variables
            where "fill" / "click"
                -> mutate page form state
]

Bot scripts ARE choreographies expressed in an imperative subset.
Each step has a precondition (previous step succeeded); failure
halts the dance — the same protocol every `<-` gate uses.

## Distinctive Innate idiom: crawl as BFS `where` domain bound is the scope fence

[web-bot[crawl {bot: @b, start-url: @u, policy: @p}]
    queue <- [@u]
    seen  <- {}
    while queue non-empty
        @current <- dequeue
        @current
            where @p:same-domain-only and host not equal to @u host -> skip
            where @current in seen                                   -> skip
            otherwise
                -> fetch, extract links, add new to queue
                -> record @current → @links in link-graph
]

The link graph IS the noosphere's structure made explicit. Vault
wiki-links are the same graph with different edge syntax. The
domain filter is the agent's scope fence; InnateScript resolvers
have the same boundary.

---

## Demo

[demo
    @bot    <- [web-bot[new]]
    @script <- [bot-script[new {name: "self-test"}]]
                 + [navigate {url: "http://localhost:8080/health"}]
                 + [assert   {check: "status:200"}]
                 + [assert   {check: "contains:ok"}]

    -> [web-bot[execute {bot: @bot, script: @script}]]
    ;; -> {steps: [...], all-passed: true}

    -> [web-bot[crawl
                  {bot: @bot,
                   start-url: "http://localhost:8080/",
                   policy: {same-domain-only: true, max-pages: 50}}]]
    ;; -> {pages-visited, link-graph: {url -> [outlinks]}}
]
